{"id": "EUVD-2026-71647", "enisaUuid": "b83486d2-1c59-3254-90fe-7a223ff2c4f7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfs: release readahead folios on iterator preparation failure\n\nnetfs_prepare_read_iterator() batches readahead folios in put_batch so that\nthe folio references can be dropped after the I/O iterator has been\nprepared.\n\nIf rolling_buffer_load_from_ra() fails after earlier folios have been\nbatched, the function returns immediately and leaves those references held.\nRelease the batch before returning the error.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T17:11:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:47:12", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9ef7c3c5cf771286f187aed199dac0972404cc0f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c148a31ca01fc160aceec777bbc0041b0d0b8bd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/935e7b74bb2368f215cf8c2ad4bff60ee4e7589e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/87eb3d272dcbcbbfe5c1576c10e5dc72810cf1f6"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80897", "GHSA-2r8v-7c33-hcr2"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "15d3431b-3dc4-3d75-8dcb-f0dc2127b31b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "256040d4-7f06-3fa3-a96e-531d1e3edb35", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14"}, {"id": "4f9199d5-d5c1-3a1d-9ffb-e529c25ed2e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.8"}, {"id": "514ee64a-9e1f-3db7-9bf1-ad727499195d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "06fa229ceb36898e68022b5654c017d2c6582d7d <2c148a31ca01fc160aceec777bbc0041b0d0b8bd"}, {"id": "655ea36f-9fb7-3c8f-ac1a-f780a91b4660", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "06fa229ceb36898e68022b5654c017d2c6582d7d <935e7b74bb2368f215cf8c2ad4bff60ee4e7589e"}, {"id": "768418a8-3175-3604-b375-5a4c4801fa04", "